codemap 9
tour feature-walk-graph
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note After a click inside the graph's canvas, the arrow keys move the selection between graph nodes instead of walking the tour: Left and Right (this feature's keys) and Up and Down (walk-steps' keys, which the graph borrows while it holds the keyboard) go to the parent, a child or a sibling lying that way first, and to the nearest node that way when none of those does. The reader reaches for it to explore the graph node by node from the keyboard instead of clicking each node (commit ad88590). A step node selects its step, an off-tour node focuses its symbol; the tree keeps its root and the camera glides to the new node over a few frames. Nothing happens while a text field holds the keyboard or when no node lies that way. Each walk is its own history place, the same rule as feature-walk-steps, so back returns to the previous node. A press outside the canvas, or hiding the Graph view, gives the arrows back to walking the tour (feature-walk-steps).

